From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:10:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(cli): every subcommand answers --help

script, process and mcp print their own usage (arguments and flags as
their parsers read them) to stdout and exit 0 for --help or -h anywhere
in their arguments. The check runs before the lane parses, so mcp --help
never starts the JSON-RPC server. Unknown flags still exit 2. The
top-level help points at `camcraft-cli <command> --help`.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/cli.rs: every_subcommand_answers_help_and_names_its_flags,
help_flag_answers_anywhere_in_the_argv, mcp_help_does_not_start_the_server,
unknown_flags_still_refuse_with_a_two_and_help_lists_per_command.

Fixes #1296

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
